# def.domain-discovery

## .what
domain discovery = exhume, unearth, discover the fundamental truth of a domain — the objects, operations, language that ALREADY EXIST beneath the surface — so code speaks the domain's own words
operative word = discover, not invent. the truth is already there, buried under surface mechanism/jargon/tool-shape. dig it out intact, do not author a convenient substitute

## .the ground truth is the real world
the truth lives in the REAL-WORLD domain — the actual practice, the people who do the work, objects/events as they exist before any software touched them. NOT in any software's description of the domain
db schema / api response / legacy class name / screen labels = a MAP, drawn by some engineer under deadline, lossy + incidental. the real-world domain = the TERRITORY. ground every term in the territory, never in a map
> the map is not the territory. the schema is not the domain.
surf instructor says "a surfer books a lesson" = ground truth. the reservations table that holds it = a poor map. name it SurfLesson (the instructor's world holds a lesson), NOT Reservation (a table stored it that way)
tell: when code's word and domain expert's word disagree, the domain expert is right. the software named its own convenience, not the domain

## .the objective
surface the domain's fundamental truth:
- true objects — nouns the domain holds (Surfer, SurfLesson), as the domain holds them, not as a table/json shapes them
- true operations — verbs the domain performs, named from WHY they exist, not HOW they run
- true language — one canonical word per concept; no synonym sprawl, no overload
a term that names the surface decays with it; a term that names the buried truth outlives every rewrite

## .buried beneath the surface
| surface (seen first) | truth beneath (discovery unearths) |
|----------------------|-------------------------------------|
| shape a db row imposes | the object the domain actually holds |
| jargon of the last tool | the word the domain expert actually says |
| HOW a step runs today | WHY the step exists at all |
| a synonym borrowed under deadline | the one canonical term |
deeper past the surface = more durable the term (name the motive; motives outlast mechanisms)

## .the test — discovered, not invented
- domain expert recognizes it with no gloss
- names what IS or why, never how
- exactly one sense in the domain
- composes: object nests, operation chains
can't point to where it already lived in the domain? you invented it — dig deeper

## .the caveat
exhume what the domain holds today; do not fabricate speculative objects (rule.prefer.wet-over-dry)
a truth you cannot yet find is a note on record, not a mandate to build

